WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510
Take a breath.

2
00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:05.350
Almost all of that air
is nitrogen and oxygen.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.110
Carbon dioxide is such
a tiny part that,

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.490
on a pie chart of the air,
its slice is too small to see.

5
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.290
Yet people keep adding more of
it, mainly by burning coal,

6
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.870
oil and gas.

7
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.870
So how can a tiny bit of one gas
change the climate of a whole

8
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.150
planet?

9
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.190
First, you'll see why coal,

10
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:30.050
oil and metal ores won't last
forever, and how recycling helps.

11
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.830
Then you'll follow carbon round
its cycle, through the air,

12
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.850
living things and the ground.

13
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.930
Your mission: explain how a little
carbon dioxide can warm the

14
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:40.820
